    {
      "op": "replace_text",
      "path": "/graph/inferences/@R001/argument/@S003/text",
      "old": "These binomial coefficients are integers (for example their usual counting interpretation as r-element subsets of a finite set proves integrality).",
      "new": "The product ratios equal the integer binomial coefficients defined in D015: for natural A≥r, count ordered lists of r distinct elements of {1,...,A}. There are A(A-1)⋯(A-r+1) such lists, and each r-element subset occurs r! times, once per ordering. Hence binom(A,r)=A(A-1)⋯(A-r+1)/r!, also for r=0 by empty products. Substituting A=λ-i+r or A=i+r gives the displayed identities and integrality."
    },
